CorvCAD patch series for KiCad 10.0.6 (caf7377), on top of 0008: let BOARD_NETLIST_UPDATER
(Update PCB from Schematic) run without the board editor, for the headless board slice.

Applied by integrations/kicad_core/fetch.py. With an editor frame nothing changes.

1. SetFootprintLoader() supplies footprints when m_frame is null; the frame's LoadFootprint is
   used otherwise.
2. Every editor-frame call (loading and exchanging footprints, the ratsnest and field style
   settings, the canvas view, OnModify, position text in display units) moves unchanged into
   the BOARD_NETLIST_UPDATER_FRAME functions of a new board_netlist_updater_frame.cpp, listed
   in pcbnew/CMakeLists.txt. The updater no longer references PCB_EDIT_FRAME members, so a
   build without the editor links it by supplying its own version of that file
   (integrations/kicad_core/headless/pcbnew/board_netlist_updater_frame.cpp).
3. Pad ratsnest visibility is only set with a frame.
4. Without a frame, a footprint whose library ID changed is exchanged through
   BOARD_NETLIST_UPDATER_FRAME::ExchangeFootprint, which a headless build supplies.
